[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From 6177a50fd32c6fd956c7265bc5297e725d221bfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Max Krummenacher <max.krummenacher@toradex.com>\nDate: Tue, 5 Jul 2022 10:58:24 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: colibri-imx6ull: fix snvs pinmux group\n\nA pin controlled by the iomuxc-snvs pin controller must be\nspecified under the dtb's iomuxc-snvs node.\n\nMove the one and only pin of that category from the iomuxc node\nand set the pinctrl-0 using it accordingly.\n\nFixes: 2aa9d6201949 (\"ARM: dts: imx6ull-colibri: add touchscreen device nodes\")\nSigned-off-by: Max Krummenacher <max.krummenacher@toradex.com>\nSigned-off-by: Shawn Guo <shawnguo@kernel.org>\n\ndiff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi\nindex 15621e03fa4d..2c3ae715c683 100644\n--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi\n+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi\n@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@ &i2c1 {\n \tatmel_mxt_ts: touchscreen@4a {\n \t\tcompatible = \"atmel,maxtouch\";\n \t\tpinctrl-names = \"default\";\n-\t\tpinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_atmel_conn>;\n+\t\tpinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_atmel_conn &pinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn>;\n \t\treg = <0x4a>;\n \t\tinterrupt-parent = <&gpio5>;\n \t\tinterrupts = <4 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;       /* SODIMM 107 / INT */\n@@ -331,7 +331,6 @@ MX6UL_PAD_ENET1_TX_EN__GPIO2_IO05       0xb0a0  /* SODIMM 30 */\n \tpinctrl_atmel_conn: atmelconngrp {\n \t\tfsl,pins = <\n \t\t\tMX6UL_PAD_JTAG_MOD__GPIO1_IO10          0xb0a0  /* SODIMM 106 */\n-\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */\n \t\t>;\n \t};\n \n@@ -684,6 +683,12 @@ MX6UL_PAD_LCD_RESET__WDOG1_WDOG_ANY    0x30b0\n };\n \n &iomuxc_snvs {\n+\tpinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn: atmelsnvsconngrp {\n+\t\tfsl,pins = <\n+\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */\n+\t\t>;\n+\t};\n+\n \tpinctrl_snvs_gpio1: snvsgpio1grp {\n \t\tfsl,pins = <\n \t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER6__GPIO5_IO06\t0x110a0\t/* SODIMM 93 */\n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n1. **File: `arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi`**\n   - **Line Changes:**\n     - The `pinctrl-0` property of the `atmel_mxt_ts` touchscreen node was modified to include a new pin control group: `&pinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn` was added alongside the existing `&pinctrl_atmel_conn`.\n     - The `pinctrl_atmel_conn` group was updated to remove the pin `MX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04`, which is now defined in a new pin control group.\n     - A new pin control group `pinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn` was created under the `&iomuxc_snvs` node, which includes the pin `MX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04`.\n\n### Relationships Between Modifications\n\n- The modification establishes a clear separation of pin control responsibilities by moving the `MX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04` pin from the `pinctrl_atmel_conn` group to a newly created `pinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn` group under the `iomuxc_snvs` node. This change ensures that the pin is correctly specified under the appropriate pin controller (`iomuxc-snvs`), addressing the bug related to pinmux configuration. The touchscreen node now references both the original and the new pin control groups, ensuring it can utilize the necessary pins correctly."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi"]}, "begin to deal with arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 22}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug was caused by the incorrect specification of a pin controlled by the iomuxc-snvs pin controller, which was not defined under the appropriate iomuxc-snvs node in the device tree. This misconfiguration led to potential issues in pin functionality for the touchscreen device, as the pin was incorrectly associated with the general iomuxc node instead of the specific snvs node.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        ARM: dts: colibri-imx6ull: fix snvs pinmux group\n\nA pin controlled by the iomuxc-snvs pin controller must be\nspecified under the dtb's iomuxc-snvs node.\n\nMove the one and only pin of that category from the iomuxc node\nand set the pinctrl-0 using it accordingly.\n\nFixes: 2aa9d6201949 (\"ARM: dts: imx6ull-colibri: add touchscreen device nodes\")\nSigned-off-by: Max Krummenacher <max.krummenacher@toradex.com>\nSigned-off-by: Shawn Guo <shawnguo@kernel.org>  \n        \n        Patch:\n         \t\tcompatible = \"atmel,maxtouch\";\n \t\tpinctrl-names = \"default\";\n-\t\tpinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_atmel_conn>;\n+\t\tpinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_atmel_conn &pinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn>;\n \t\treg = <0x4a>;\n \t\tinterrupt-parent = <&gpio5>;\n \t\tfsl,pins = <\n \t\t\tMX6UL_PAD_JTAG_MOD__GPIO1_IO10          0xb0a0  /* SODIMM 106 */\n-\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */\n \t\t>;\n \t};\n \n &iomuxc_snvs {\n+\tpinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn: atmelsnvsconngrp {\n+\t\tfsl,pins = <\n+\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */\n+\t\t>;\n+\t};\n+\n \tpinctrl_snvs_gpio1: snvsgpio1grp {\n \t\tfsl,pins = <\n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n-\t\tpinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_atmel_conn>;\n-\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */\n+\tpinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_atmel_conn &pinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn>;\n+\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */\n+\tpinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn: atmelsnvsconngrp {\n+\t\tfsl,pins = <\n+\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */\n+\t\t>;"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "-\t\tpinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_atmel_conn>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi", "lineno": 169, "induce_cid": "2aa9d6201949b07dca7951710ef3be995600216c"}, {"buggy_stmt": "-\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi", "lineno": 334, "induce_cid": "2aa9d6201949b07dca7951710ef3be995600216c"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\t\tMX6ULL_PAD_SNVS_TAMPER4__GPIO5_IO04     0xb0a0\t/* SODIMM 107 */", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi", "lineno": 334, "induce_cid": "2aa9d6201949b07dca7951710ef3be995600216c"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tpinctrl_atmel_snvs_conn: atmelsnvsconngrp {", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi", "lineno": 331, "induce_cid": "2aa9d6201949b07dca7951710ef3be995600216c"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tfsl,pins = <", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6ull-colibri.dtsi", "lineno": 316, "induce_cid": "3f781d5c67f7f5763913cccb972598df19f80c06"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tfsl,pins = <", "fi